A||||5||jlhuber||what the *@$% !?!?||||8||
Z||000000||jlhuber||02-02-2000||12:03 AM||||man, i feel like a complete a$$ now.  with the motor running, my gt made some god-awful knocking/rattling sounds.  i consulted a mechanic buddy for his opinion.  we both agreeed and were quite confident that the motor most likely had a broken valve or a loose rod.  but we decided to get another friend's opinion before we start to tear into the motor.  i start it up for him to listen to, and not a minute later he says hang on, i'll be right back.  he dissapers and promptly returns holding a large prybar.  my imediate thoughts are what the #%$@ is he going to do!?  he sticks the prybar in the engine bay, wiggles it arround a bit and says here's your problem, your alternator has come loose and is rattling on various metal parts near-by it.  what!? that's it!? i was about 5 minutes from dissasembling part of the motor which would have accomplished nothing!?!  tightened the lower alternator mounting bolt, and it runs/sounds fine now, except that i have a bad oil pump.  moral of the story, if it ain't broken, don't fix it.  don't tear down a motor that has what someone might say is a rod knock, loose rocker arm, or even a broken valve, check for loose nuts, bolts, and acessories first.  well, that was my excitement for the day.  oh yeah, there was also this hot chick flirting with me at the shop, but that is another story.  oh well, tomorrow's another day, and i'm tired so i'm going to bed.  ||||reg||8
Z||000001||fierospeeder||02-02-2000||12:40 AM||||was she flirting with you for your brains or for your fiero?<P>This is similiar to your story, my mom has a celebrity 2.8l station wagon.  The car stalled and wouldn't want to start.  The starter would click and you can tell it was draining the battery power but the engine wouldn't turn over.  Friends were saying the starter was bad, or something like the crankshaft locked up and we had to take the engine apart.  My moms friend whose son is a mechanic didn't have the correct answer.  We were gonna take the engine apart to check it over more and got the belt off.  I was playing around and saw that the alternator pulley wasn't turning.  The bearings got shot and it caused enough resistance to prevent the engine from starting.  <BR>Advice listener beware!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phaeton||02-02-2000||02:12 AM||||Thats one of the great things about this forum:  reality checks.  Put a problem out there and roughly 23 answers are sent in, most all of them good. Then comes the feedback with the physical truth of the matter and sometimes nobody got it right.  If I easily learned humility I wouldn't be driving a Fiero, but I am filling some of the large gaps in knowledge suddenly appearing right in the spot formerly taken by Everything There Is To Know. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||SpeedPhreak||02-02-2000||11:15 AM||||i agree, i belong to several forums cause i like expensive hobbies.  i must say that this one is the best...not only for help but it really feels like we are a tighter group of people instead of a few regulars that just answer questions of new & 1 time visitors day in & day out...know what i mean?<P>i know i probably would not want to handle much of the maintainence/repair with out this group.||||reg||1
Z||000004||shaolin||02-02-2000||11:11 PM||||Similar Story:<BR>We are out running a jeep thru the river and sand at a local 4WD spot. been here all day playing. Hit the river at a spot that is, all but shallow. Jeep stops and we get stuck. Bigfoot's little brother has to pull us out. Now where we are there is no such thing as calling a tow truck, you see the jeep is not starting, and it's getting late. Well, a couple of guys that look like they know what they are doing come along. Oh you fried your starter. So they give us a ride into town. We get back, play in the sand and get all dirty, but we get it on. No go....Hours later VERY LATE....VERY DARK.... Late night 4x4's come along, these guys know what they are doing....HYDROSTATIC LOCK!!!!!!! 10 minutse and we are uo and running. I like the moral to your story....now I am going to bed as well....||||reg||1
Z||000005||jlhuber||02-03-2000||06:12 PM||||SHAOLIN,  i actually had similar experience.  i was 'wheelin here in New Jersey with a buddy of mine.  he had a '99 wrangler stock, and i had a '89 ford ranger slightly modified.  get this, i got stuck and he could pull me out no problem, but when he got stuck all i could do was spin.  course it didn't help that i needed new tires, and that he was high centered on a log, and that upon further inspection, we noticed that the "little water puddle" had a bed of clay.  the jeep had the front half of the motor submerged in the water for the better part of 9 hours before some "real" jeeps came and gave us a hand.  we thought an alien spacecraft was coming over the hill, (we were in what used to be a natural lake, but it dried up a little) though it turned out to be a few modified jeeps with excellent off-road lighting.  2 minutes after they got us out (it took two of them to break the vacume that the clay was creating) the jeep was back on the trail headded home.  the stuck jeep was also hydrolocked, and i got mud in the ranger's started and burned it up.  oh well, it was fun.||||reg||1
